  "id": "wrapparty",
  "neon": "#ff4d4d",
  "note": "WRAP PARTY — the back-door pub for the studio block, on Foundry Way.\n\nThe tile's prose: it opens at eleven at night and does its best trade at two in the morning, so it\nhas no window worth the name. One door, a red bulb over it that is on when the bar is, and a brass\nplate by the handle reading WRAP PARTY with EVERY NIGHT scratched underneath.\n\nThe frontage is on the entrance side, Foundry Way; it used to be authored on the back wall, so the\nstreet saw a blank box. The front is two blind brick bays with the door between them under a short\nhood and the red bulb, the brass plate beside it, and the upper windows blacked out. The blade at the\ncorner is the only thing on the street you can find in the dark; it is a `bladePanel`, world\ngeometry hung proud of the wall, rather than the screen-space `neonBlade` it used to be. A fire escape comes down\nthe flank, because the rooms upstairs are where the band sleeps it off.\n\nThe walls are brick (`ty_regerts`, `ty_reel_flank`). They were `ty_bar_b` and `ty_bar_a`,\nwhich are in the window-grid family, and a grid of lit windows is exactly what this bar hasn't got.",
  "pal": "ty_regerts",
